@Silveryon
If you've never made a complete game, then it's smart to start with a relatively simple story like you're planning.  So don't worry too much about it not be original and instead focus on making it fun to play.  Maybe focus on one major mechanic that you want to implement, just to keep the project from growing too large for you to actually finish.
As for making your own assets, trouble time is right that you don't need any art experience, but it sure can help.  I'd suggest not trying to make everything by yourself at first, and instead start with learning how to edit the defaults.  It'll help you learn how the assets work in the engine and keep the graphics from overwhelming you, since it can take a lot of time to make all that you need.

