@Jackkel Dragon
The type of game your describing used to be really popular actually, well something similar. I reccomend you look into various old point and click adventure games and look at what worked for them and try to transpose it into RPG Maker and that may help your game out and put your mind at ease.
@gigaswardblade
I notice you do a whole lot of world building in your posts here. Really, as you mentioned, there isn't too much people can comment about on it. I do notice that there are a Ton of races in that world, how cosmopolitan is this world? Like I think that how these races interact with one another might allow for more discussion than just their histories.
@Kittyplaysgameswithstring
I think I need more information to make an informed comment on this, but wouldn't defeating senpai be easy, getting senpai to notice you is hard so you'd basically have invisiblity.
@Sami-Fire64
I like the premise, but the name Fwillra seems a bit hard to pronunce, then again I have a character name Iii (pronounced like Ai) so I have no room to judge. as with Jackkel Dragon, I'd reccomend looking for inspiration in point and click games unless you're looking to have combat gameplay.
@captainette777
I think a boss rush game could work very well, all you need is some heavy focus on making each and every boss challenging enough that people feel like they had to think through each battle. I'd reccomend you use regenerating resources or cooldowns to manage skills so its harder to end up in situations where its impossible to win and you just slowly bleed down(I assume you'll find a way to make skills integral to battles)
@pandadodod
it sounds a little overdone, the traditional "subversisve" fairy tale type thing. Still it can be done, it really depends on how its executed.
@gigaswardblade
Looking at your character designs seem alright, at the very least they seem varied besides those 4 on the bottom of the first one. Personally I think the cast is a little big but that's just me.
