it's funny that you guys are talking about world sizes and stuff now, because I came back just to ask some of the readers of this thread's opinion on a simple idea I have for a separate project of mine:
Instead of a sprawling RPG world or main overworld, I was going to have a story take place in a future where they can simply teleport to 7 different Hubworlds with their own dungeon levels full of monsters in them. I'm not sure if that was a fun idea or not, or people would think it was uninspired or lazy if I decided to have a teleporter room that simply took you to wherever you want, or clunky if I don't. Sorry if it sounds so basic, I'm just new to game design that appeals to people other than me for once.
